r of 1983, and quickly becomes inseparable friends with schoolmates Rena Ryuuguu, Mion Sonozaki, Satoko Houjou, and Rika Furude. However, darkness lurks underneath the seemingly idyllic life they lead.\n\nAs the village prepares for its annual festival, Keiichi learns about the local legends surrounding it. To his horror, he discovers that there have been several murders and disappearances in the village in the recent years, and that they all seem to be connected to the festival and the village's patron god, Oyashiro. Keiichi tries to ask his new friends about these incidents, but they are suspiciously silent and refuse to give him the answers he needs. As more and more bizarre events occur, he wonders just what else his friends might be keeping from him, and if he can even trust them at all.\n\nWhen madness and paranoia begin taking root in Keiichi's heart, he will stumble straight into the mysteries at work in Higurashi no Naku Koro ni, a story that is told across multiple arcs.\n\n(Source: MAL Rewrite)\n\nNote: Based on the amateur mystery game by 07th Expansion, the story is told in a series of different scenarios."},"tags":[{"name":"Denpa","rank":98,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Alternate Universe","rank":96,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Ensemble Cast","rank":94,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Time Manipulation","rank":92,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Tragedy","rank":89,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Conspiracy","rank":87,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Rural","rank":86,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Achronological Order","rank":85,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Gore","rank":84,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Time Loop","rank":83,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Body Horror","rank":74,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Bullying","rank":73,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Torture","rank":73,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Urban Fantasy","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Yandere","rank":69,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Twins","rank":69,"spoiler":true},{"name":"Chibi","rank":68,"spoiler":false